Overview

Built and organized a rack-based homelab environment focused on clean infrastructure, power protection, cable management, expandability, and reliable hardware deployment.

Components

Power Backup | UPS
Rack Hardware | Blank Panels
Cabling | Keystone Jacks
Storage | Rack Shelves
Networking | Smart Switch
Systems | 2 Chassis Installed
Accessory | Raspberry Pi Case

Process

Installed and organized rack hardware to create a clean and functional homelab setup. Added a UPS for backup power and surge protection. Mounted shelves and chassis systems for equipment placement. Installed blank panels to improve airflow and rack appearance. Added keystone jacks for structured cable routing and easier network management. Integrated the smart switch for centralized connectivity and placed the Raspberry Pi into a protective case for long-term use. Verified cable routing, airflow, and overall equipment accessibility.

